CLASSIFICATION BOUNDARIES
Queue wait ≠ resolution delay. Device failure ≠ stock shortage. Permissions ≠ network connection. Issue never fixed ≠ issue fixed then returned. Friendliness ≠ technical expertise. Clear explanations ≠ progress updates. A duration alone does not establish sentiment. “Excellent service” -> Overall Appreciation / General Satisfaction or Dissatisfaction, not unsupported claims about speed or competence. “Friendly staff but my issue remains unresolved” -> positive Reception Quality + negative Resolution Outcome.

CONTROLLED EXCEPTIONS
If a theme fits but no sub-theme does, use that theme and Other Reason (Review Required). If no official theme fits, use theme Other Topics (Review Required) and sub-theme Out of Taxonomy (Review Required). Last resort ONLY: not for synonyms, minor details, uncertainty or generic praise. Do not invent labels. Explain the gap (and optional proposal) in the existing justification, in English. Never expand the taxonomy automatically; exceptions must be rare and filterable by “Review Required”.

SEVERITY, SIGNALS, CONFIDENCE & VISIT TYPE
Severity (not emotional intensity): Low = none/minor; Warning = limited issue; High = significant operational disruption or repeated failed interventions described in the comment; Critical = explicit major disruption, urgent serious risk or severe impact. Severity never triggers alerts. Signals only if supported: Aggression = explicit hostility; Abandonment = stated intent to give up; Loss of Trust = explicit loss of confidence. Otherwise use schema-approved empty values. Do NOT calculate cross-visit recurrence; repeated visits mentioned in this ONE comment may appear in its category/justification. Confidence (0–1) = clarity/evidential support, not severity or satisfaction. Prefer supplied structured visit type: Appointment, Incident, Information, Returned Hardware; if absent use the schema-approved unknown/default.

JUSTIFICATIONS & FINAL CHECK
Write concise factual ENGLISH justifications explaining classifications and preserving meaningful facts and impacts. No invented causes or conclusions. Verify exact label-to-theme mapping; appropriate polarity; no duplication; rare justified exceptions; faithful comment_EN; English generated text; consistent scores; NO emails, counter lookup or historical recurrence; valid schema-compliant JSON ONLY.
